== 6. Reading the panels ======================================= 
  THE POINT OF THE FIGURE: PRAME marks the melanoma compartment and 
  should fill it densely. RASSF9 should NOT follow it -- if script 
  30's lineage result is right, RASSF9 appears scattered across the 
  whole section, including dermis and adnexal structures, with no 
  enrichment in the tumour. 
 
  WHAT WOULD CONTRADICT IT: RASSF9 tracking PRAME, or RASSF9 
  concentrated in the nevus region specifically. Either would mean 
  the pseudobulk summary is hiding spatial structure, and would need 
  explaining before the figure is used. 
 
  CAUTION ON READING SPARSE GENES SPATIALLY: RASSF9 is detected in 
  11% of spots. A scattered appearance is partly sparsity and not 
  only biology, so the figure ILLUSTRATES the quantified result in 
  script 30 section 4 -- it does not independently establish it, and 
  the legend must say so. 
